        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f5641e59-4585-5ea7-a975-0e2824593fa7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ahmad Niyaltigin, Mas'ud I of Ghazni, Mahmud of Ghazni, Mohammad\n- Roles: treasurer, sultan, heir\n- Organizations: Ghaznavid Empire\n\nFacts:\n- Ahmad Niyaltigin was a treasurer of Sultan Mahmud Ghaznavi and later of Mahmud's son Sultan Mas'ud Ghaznavi.\n- Mas'ud I of Ghazni was born in 998.\n- Upon the death of Mahmud of Ghazni, Mohammad had been nominated as heir, but Mas'ud I of Ghazni seized the Ghaznavid throne from his younger twin Mohammad.\n- Mas'ud I of Ghazni was sultan of the Ghaznavid Empire from 1030 to 1040.\n- Mas'ud I of Ghazni was known as Amīr-i Shahīd, meaning \"the martyr king.\"\n- Mas'ud I of Ghazni died on 17 January 1040.",
